{"scope": "Replay unchanged v7 JSON in current native retrieval/validation; no Provider.\n\nThis is offline compatibility and partial-result verification, not a new live\ngeneration or a change to the original failed operation receipts.\n", "providerCalls": 0, "taskWrites": 0, "indexWrites": 0, "beforeHash": "4708c07a18e305c6aed2bdb183e439ba2de02fcd5ccfa8dc867b44afbf1bf3f9", "afterHash": "4708c07a18e305c6aed2bdb183e439ba2de02fcd5ccfa8dc867b44afbf1bf3f9", "results": {"critique": {"status": "success", "partial": true, "message": "**部分分析**\n\n向量量化方面，作者报告对所有属性（尤其位置、旋转、尺度）量化会导致显著精度损失，离散表示精度明显下降；因此仅对SH系数中全局显著性最低的元素进行VQ，位置、形状、旋转和不透明度等关键属性跳过VQ并以float16存储。其压缩收益限于低显著SH子集，且依赖相近外观的高斯子组假设，对非SH属性未能压缩。 [1] [2]\n\n<details>\n<summary>尚待确认</summary>\n\n另有2项判断暂未确认，未纳入本次结论。\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>待核查问题</summary>\n\n- 待核查：15倍压缩与200+FPS是否在论文其他章节有明确原始声明，还是仅由表1核对行推算；合成目标级数据集的性能数字是否支持这些主张。\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>原文依据</summary>\n\n- [1] “Our empirical findings indicate that applying quantization across all elements-especially for attributes like position, rotation, and scale-results in significant accuracy losses and a marked reduction in precision when represented discretely.”\n- [1] “Based on this, we apply VQ selectively on the least significant elements in the Spherical Harmonics (SHs).”\n- [2] “To preserve essential attributes, including Spherical Harmonics with higher global significance scores, along with Gaussian position, shape, rotation, and opacity, we skip VQ for these elements and store them directly in float16 format.”\n- [1] “We propose applying VQ to the Spherical Harmonics (SH) coefficients, based on the assumption that a subgroup of 3d Gaussians typically exhibits a similar appearance.”\n\n</details>", "summary": "向量量化方面，作者报告对所有属性（尤其位置、旋转、尺度）量化会导致显著精度损失，离散表示精度明显下降；因此仅对SH系数中全局显著性最低的元素进行VQ，位置、形状、旋转和不透明度等关键属性跳过VQ并以float16存储。其压缩收益限于低显著SH子集，且依赖相近外观的高斯子组假设，对非SH属性未能压缩。 [1] [2]", "groundedClaims": [{"summary": "向量量化方面，作者报告对所有属性（尤其位置、旋转、尺度）量化会导致显著精度损失，离散表示精度明显下降；因此仅对SH系数中全局显著性最低的元素进行VQ，位置、形状、旋转和不透明度等关键属性跳过VQ并以float16存储。其压缩收益限于低显著SH子集，且依赖相近外观的高斯子组假设，对非SH属性未能压缩。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-19", "quote": "Our empirical findings indicate that applying quantization across all elements-especially for attributes like position, rotation, and scale-results in significant accuracy losses and a marked reduction in precision when represented discretely."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-19", "quote": "Based on this, we apply VQ selectively on the least significant elements in the Spherical Harmonics (SHs)."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "To preserve essential attributes, including Spherical Harmonics with higher global significance scores, along with Gaussian position, shape, rotation, and opacity, we skip VQ for these elements and store them directly in float16 format."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-19", "quote": "We propose applying VQ to the Spherical Harmonics (SH) coefficients, based on the assumption that a subgroup of 3d Gaussians typically exhibits a similar appearance."}], "section": "weakness"}], "pendingQuestions": ["待核查：15倍压缩与200+FPS是否在论文其他章节有明确原始声明，还是仅由表1核对行推算；合成目标级数据集的性能数字是否支持这些主张。"], "rag_sources": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-19", "text": "high compression rates. However, quantizing Gaussian attributes in a point-based, inherently non-Euclidean representation poses notable challenges. Our empirical findings indicate that applying quantization across all elements-especially for attributes like position, rotation, and scale-results in significant accuracy losses and a marked reduction in precision when represented discretely.\nWe propose applying VQ to the Spherical Harmonics (SH) coefficients, based on the assumption that a subgroup of 3d Gaussians typically exhibits a similar appearance. Fundamentally, VQ segments the Gaussians G = {g 1 , g 2 , . . . , g N } (here we apply it on SH) to the K codes in the codebook C = {c 1 , c 2 , . . . , c K }, where each g j , c k ∈ R d and K ≪ N. d means SH dimension. We aim to strike a balance between rendering quality loss and compression rate by leveraging the pre-computed significance score from Eq. 3. Based on this, we apply VQ selectively on the least significant elements in the Spherical Harmonics (SHs). Specifically, we initialize C via K-means, iteratively sample a batch of G, associates them to the closest codes by euclidean distance, and update each c k via moving average rule:", "metadata": {"title": "LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS", "chunk_index": 19, "page_index": 4, "section_id": "section-7", "id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "section_title": "Gaussian Attributes Vector Quantization", "index_version": "2977684d0da4a8b6", "page": 5, "file_name": "public-light.pdf"}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunkIndex": 19, "pageIndex": 4, "sectionId": "section-7", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "text": "method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations. For fair metric and visual comparison, we re-trained 3D-GS and Compressed 3D-GS[34]using their original code and configurations on our platform (NVIDIA A6000 GPU), with results marked by * . For a full dynamic viewpoint comparison, please see our supplementary video.\ncode vector using a moving average. We fine-tune the codebook for 5,000 iterations, while fixing the gaussian-to-codebook mapping. We disable additional clone/split operations and leverage photometric loss on the training views. To preserve essential attributes, including Spherical Harmonics with higher global significance scores, along with Gaussian position, shape, rotation, and opacity, we skip VQ for these elements and store them directly in float16 format.\nEquation: c k = λ d • c k + (1 − λ d ) • 1/T k • gj ∈R(c k ) GS j • g j , where T k = gj ∈R(c k ) GS j", "metadata": {"chunk_index": 21, "page_index": 4, "section_id": "section-7", "page": 5, "title": "LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS", "id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "file_name": "public-light.pdf", "index_version": "2977684d0da4a8b6", "section_title": "Gaussian Attributes Vector Quantization"}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunkIndex": 21, "pageIndex": 4, "sectionId": "section-7", "sourceType": "current_paper"}], "resolved_from": "pdf_id", "pdf_id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "traceId": "d45bd6c7-02e2-49cf-9fc3-d28553939c69"}, "compose": {"status": "success", "message": "**部分比较**\n\n在3DGS中，场景由一组3D高斯表示，每个高斯包含位置、透明度/不透明度参数α和协方差Σ。论文同时优化球谐系数来表示颜色c，以捕捉视角相关的外观。 [1] [2]\n\n推断：原始3DGS通过密集各向异性高斯优化和快速光栅化追求高质量与实时渲染；LightGaussian则在3DGS基础上引入剪枝、低阶球谐蒸馏与矢量量化，以较小视觉质量代价换取更小的表示规模和更高FPS。 [3] [2] [4] [5] [6] [7]\n\n\n| 维度 | 论文 1 | 论文 2 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 表示规模/存储 | 原始3DGS报告其各向异性高斯能够以较少参数建模复杂形状，但现有片段未给出与LightGaussian同条件的存储规模对比。 [8] | LightGaussian作者报告大幅压缩（原文示例从782MB到45MB），并在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007。（作者报告，未作同条件比较） [7] |\n| 渲染速度 | 原始3DGS报告在1080p分辨率下实现实时新视角合成，给出作者主张的≥30 fps阈值。（作者报告，未作同条件比较） [3] | LightGaussian作者报告在复杂场景上渲染速度提升至超过200 FPS。（作者报告，未作同条件比较） [7] |\n| 质量/视觉保真度 | 原始3DGS报告其辐射场质量与质量最佳的先前方法相当，并称在较长训练下达到最先进质量。 [9] | 作者报告在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007，并称方法在FPS、模型大小与渲染质量之间取得最佳平衡。（作者报告，未作同条件比较） [7] [10] |\n| 取舍机制 | 原始3DGS通过各向异性协方差优化与密度控制构造精确场景，并开发可见性感知渲染以加速训练与支持实时渲染。 [2] | LightGaussian通过全局显著性剪枝、从全阶球谐教师到低阶学生的蒸馏以及矢量量化来减少冗余，从而在规模、速度和质量之间取得平衡。 [4] [5] [6] |\n\n<details>\n<summary>比较范围</summary>\n\nLightGaussian正文章节中的表格存在列跨度和未核对列映射，因此未使用这些表格数值进行直接排序；速度与存储数字来自不同场景/条件，不能直接拼接比较。；当前片段未提供两篇论文在同一硬件、同一数据集下完整逐项对齐的实验表，因此比较以作者报告和定性推断为主。\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>原文依据</summary>\n\n- 论文 1：3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering\n- 论文 2：LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS\n- [1] “In addition to positions 𝑝, 𝛼, and covariance Σ, we also optimize SH coefficients representing color 𝑐 of each Gaussian to correctly capture the view-dependent appearance of the scene.”\n- [2] “First, starting from sparse points produced during camera calibration, we represent the scene with 3D Gaussians that preserve desirable properties of continuous volumetric radiance fields for scene optimization while avoiding unnecessary computation in empty space;”\n- [3] “We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution.”\n- [2] “Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;”\n- [4] “pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy.”\n- [5] “Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs.”\n- [6] “of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation.”\n- [7] “This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360).”\n- [7] “Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes.”\n- [8] “In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters.”\n- [9] “Our method achieves real-time rendering of radiance fields with quality that equals the previous method with the best quality[Barron et al. 2022], while only requiring optimization times competitive with the fastest previous methods[Fridovich-Keil and Yu et al. 2022;Müller et al. 2022].”\n- [9] “Note that for comparable training times to InstantNGP[Müller et al. 2022], we achieve similar quality to theirs; while this is the maximum quality they reach, by training for 51min we achieve state-of-the-art quality, even slightly better than Mip-NeRF360[Barron et al. 2022].”\n- [10] “method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations.”\n- [2] “Third, we develop a fast visibility-aware rendering algorithm that supports anisotropic splatting and both accelerates training and allows realtime rendering.”\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>尚待确认</summary>\n\n另有1项判断暂未确认，未纳入本次结论。\n\n</details>", "partial": true, "claims": [{"summary": "在3DGS中，场景由一组3D高斯表示，每个高斯包含位置、透明度/不透明度参数α和协方差Σ。论文同时优化球谐系数来表示颜色c，以捕捉视角相关的外观。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-34", "quote": "In addition to positions 𝑝, 𝛼, and covariance Σ, we also optimize SH coefficients representing color 𝑐 of each Gaussian to correctly capture the view-dependent appearance of the scene."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "First, starting from sparse points produced during camera calibration, we represent the scene with 3D Gaussians that preserve desirable properties of continuous volumetric radiance fields for scene optimization while avoiding unnecessary computation in empty space;"}]}, {"summary": "原始3DGS通过密集各向异性高斯优化和快速光栅化追求高质量与实时渲染；LightGaussian则在3DGS基础上引入剪枝、低阶球谐蒸馏与矢量量化，以较小视觉质量代价换取更小的表示规模和更高FPS。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "quote": "of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes."}]}, {"summary": "原始3DGS报告其各向异性高斯能够以较少参数建模复杂形状，但现有片段未给出与LightGaussian同条件的存储规模对比。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian作者报告大幅压缩（原文示例从782MB到45MB），并在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}, {"summary": "原始3DGS报告在1080p分辨率下实现实时新视角合成，给出作者主张的≥30 fps阈值。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian作者报告在复杂场景上渲染速度提升至超过200 FPS。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f633