ussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian作者报告大幅压缩（原文示例从782MB到45MB），并在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}]}, {"label": "渲染速度", "cells": [{"summary": "原始3DGS报告在1080p分辨率下实现实时新视角合成，给出作者主张的≥30 fps阈值。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian作者报告在复杂场景上渲染速度提升至超过200 FPS。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}]}, {"label": "质量/视觉保真度", "cells": [{"summary": "原始3DGS报告其辐射场质量与质量最佳的先前方法相当，并称在较长训练下达到最先进质量。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0", "quote": "Our method achieves real-time rendering of radiance fields with quality that equals the previous method with the best quality[Barron et al. 2022], while only requiring optimization times competitive with the fastest previous methods[Fridovich-Keil and Yu et al. 2022;Müller et al. 2022]."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0", "quote": "Note that for comparable training times to InstantNGP[Müller et al. 2022], we achieve similar quality to theirs; while this is the maximum quality they reach, by training for 51min we achieve state-of-the-art quality, even slightly better than Mip-NeRF360[Barron et al. 2022]."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "作者报告在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007，并称方法在FPS、模型大小与渲染质量之间取得最佳平衡。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}]}, {"label": "取舍机制", "cells": [{"summary": "原始3DGS通过各向异性协方差优化与密度控制构造精确场景，并开发可见性感知渲染以加速训练与支持实时渲染。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Third, we develop a fast visibility-aware rendering algorithm that supports anisotropic splatting and both accelerates training and allows realtime rendering."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian通过全局显著性剪枝、从全阶球谐教师到低阶学生的蒸馏以及矢量量化来减少冗余，从而在规模、速度和质量之间取得平衡。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "quote": "of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}]}], "rag_sources": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0", "text": "Paper: 3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering\n\nSection: Ours (93 fps)\n\nContent:\nTrain: 51min, PSNR: 25.2 Fig.1. Our method achieves real-time rendering of radiance fields with quality that equals the previous method with the best quality[Barron et al. 2022], while only requiring optimization times competitive with the fastest previous methods[Fridovich-Keil and Yu et al. 2022;Müller et al. 2022]. Key to this performance is a novel 3D Gaussian scene representation coupled with a real-time differentiable renderer, which offers significant speedup to both scene optimization and novel view synthesis. Note that for comparable training times to InstantNGP[Müller et al. 2022], we achieve similar quality to theirs; while this is the maximum quality they reach, by training for 51min we achieve state-of-the-art quality, even slightly better than Mip-NeRF360[Barron et al. 2022].", "metadata": {"page_index": 0, "file_name": "target_paper.pdf", "section_id": "section-1", "section_title": "Ours (93 fps)", "title": "3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering", "chunk_index": 0, "id": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "page": 1}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "chunkIndex": 0, "pageIndex": 0, "sectionId": "section-1", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "text": "Paper: 3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering\n\nSection: Ours (93 fps)\n\nContent:\na real-time differentiable renderer, which offers significant speedup to both scene optimization and novel view synthesis. Note that for comparable training times to InstantNGP[Müller et al. 2022], we achieve similar quality to theirs; while this is the maximum quality they reach, by training for 51min we achieve state-of-the-art quality, even slightly better than Mip-NeRF360[Barron et al. 2022].\nRadiance Field methods have recently revolutionized novel-view synthesis of scenes captured with multiple photos or videos.\nHowever, achieving high visual quality still requires neural networks that are costly to train and render, while recent faster methods inevitably trade off speed for quality.\nFor unbounded and complete scenes (rather than isolated objects) and 1080p resolution rendering, no current method can achieve real-time display rates.\nWe introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution.", "metadata": {"id": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "section_title": "Ours (93 fps)", "page_index": 0, "section_id": "section-1", "page": 1, "title": "3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering", "chunk_index": 1, "file_name": "target_paper.pdf"}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "chunkIndex": 1, "pageIndex": 0, "sectionId": "section-1", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "text": "Paper: 3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering\n\nSection: Ours (93 fps)\n\nContent:\nWe introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution.\nFirst, starting from sparse points produced during camera calibration, we represent the scene with 3D Gaussians that preserve desirable properties of continuous volumetric radiance fields for scene optimization while avoiding unnecessary computation in empty space;\nSecond, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;\nThird, we develop a fast visibility-aware rendering algorithm that supports anisotropic splatting and both accelerates training and allows realtime rendering.\nWe demonstrate state-of-the-art visual quality and real-time rendering on several established datasets.\nCCS Concepts: • Computing methodologies → Rendering; Point-based models; Rasterization; Machine learning approaches.", "metadata": {"chunk_index": 2, "section_title": "Ours (93 fps)", "page_index": 0, "title": "3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering", "page": 1, "file_name": "target_paper.pdf", "section_id": "section-1", "id": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "chunkIndex": 2, "pageIndex": 0, "sectionId": "section-1", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-34", "text": "Paper: 3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering\n\nSection: OPTIMIZATION WITH ADAPTIVE DENSITY CONTROL OF 3D GAUSSIANS\n\nContent:\nThe core of our approach is the optimization step, which creates a dense set of 3D Gaussians accurately representing the scene for free-view synthesis. In addition to positions 𝑝, 𝛼, and covariance Σ, we also optimize SH coefficients representing color 𝑐 of each Gaussian to correctly capture the view-dependent appearance of the scene. The optimization of these parameters is interleaved with steps that control the density of the Gaussians to better represent the scene.", "metadata": {"chunk_index": 34, "page": 4, "file_name": "target_paper.pdf", "section_id": "section-9", "title": "3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering", "page_index": 3, "id": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "section_title": "OPTIMIZATION WITH ADAPTIVE DENSITY CONTROL OF 3D GAUSSIANS"}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "chunkIndex": 34, "pageIndex": 3, "sectionId": "section-9", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "text": "Paper: 3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering\n\nSection: Results and Evaluation\n\nContent:\nWe report and compare our achieved PSNR scores with previous methods in Table2using a white background for compatibility.\nExamples can be seen in Fig.10(second image from the left) and in supplemental material.\nThe trained synthetic scenes rendered at 180-300 FPS.\nCompactness. In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters. We showcase this by evaluating our approach against the highly compact, point-based models obtained by[Zhang et al. 2022]. We start from their initial point cloud which is obtained by space carving with foreground masks and optimize until we break even with their reported PSNR scores. This usually happens within 2-4 minutes. We surpass their reported metrics using approximately one-fourth of their point count, resulting in an average model size of 3.8 MB, as opposed to their 9 MB. We note that for this experiment, we only used two degrees of our spherical harmonics, similar to theirs.", "metadata": {"file_name": "target_paper.pdf", "chunk_index": 64, "section_title": "Results and Evaluation", "section_id": "section-18", "page": 8, "id": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "title": "3D Gaussian Splatting for Real-Time Radiance Field Rendering", "page_index": 7}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf", "chunkIndex": 64, "pageIndex": 7, "sectionId": "section-18", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "text": "Paper: LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS\n\nSection: Gaussian Pruning & Recovery\n\nContent:\npruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy. Identifying redundant yet recoverable Gaussians is essential to our approach. However, pruning Gaussians based on simple criteria (e.g., point opacity) risks degrading modeling performance, as it may eliminate essential scene details, as shown in Fig.3.\nGlobal Significance Calculation.\nInspired by Eq.\n2, we go beyond using Gaussian opacity alone to assess significance by evaluating 3D Gaussians within the view frustum, projecting them onto the camera viewpoint for rendering.\nThe initial significance score of each Gaussian (denoted as G(X j )) can then be quantified based on its contribution to each pixel (ray, r i ) across all training views using the criteria 1(G(X j ), r i ) whether they intersect or not.\nConsequently, we iterate over all training pixels to calculate the hit count of each Gaussian.\nThe score is further refined by the adjusted 3D Gaussian's volume γ (Σ j ) and 3D Gaussian's opacity σ j , as they all contribute for the rendering formula.\nThe volume calculation equation of the j-th 3D Guassian is V(Σ j ) = 4 3 πabc, where abc are the 3 dimensions of Scale (S).", "metadata": {"id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "file_name": "public-light.pdf", "title": "LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS", "section_id": "section-5", "index_version": "2977684d0da4a8b6", "page": 4, "chunk_index": 13, "section_title": "Gaussian Pruning & Recovery", "page_index": 3}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunkIndex": 13, "pageIndex": 3, "sectionId": "section-5", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "text": "Paper: LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS\n\nSection: Distilling into Compact SHs\n\nContent:\nscene quality, we introduce a knowledge distillation approach. Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs. Supervision is based on the difference in predicted pixel intensities between the two models, with images synthesized at camera positions by sampling around each training view according to a Gaussian distribution:\n(5)\nwhere R and t denote rendering camera rotation and position, t pseudo and t train represent the newly synthesized and training camera positions, respectively. N denotes a Gaussian distribution with mean 0 and variance σ 2 , which is added to the original position to generate the new position.\nEquation: L distill = 1 HW HW i=1 ∥C teacher (r i ; [R|t]) − C student (r i ; [R|t])∥ 2 2 .\nEquation: t pseudo = t train + N (0, σ 2 ),(6)", "metadata": {"section_id": "section-6", "id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunk_index": 17, "page_index": 4, "index_version": "2977684d0da4a8b6", "page": 5, "section_title": "Distilling into Compact SHs", "title": "LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS", "file_name": "public-light.pdf"}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunkIndex": 17, "pageIndex": 4, "sectionId": "section-6", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "text": "Paper: LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS\n\nSection: Gaussian Attributes Vector Quantization\n\nContent:\nmethod strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations. For fair metric and visual comparison, we re-trained 3D-GS and Compressed 3D-GS[34]using their original code and configurations on our platform (NVIDIA A6000 GPU), with results marked by * . For a full dynamic viewpoint comparison, please see our supplementary video.\ncode vector using a moving average. We fine-tune the codebook for 5,000 iterations, while fixing the gaussian-to-codebook mapping. We disable additional clone/split operations and leverage photometric loss on the training views. To preserve essential attributes, including Spherical Harmonics with higher global significance scores, along with Gaussian position, shape, rotation, and opacity, we skip VQ for these elements and store them directly in float16 format.\nEquation: c k = λ d • c k + (1 − λ d ) • 1/T k • gj ∈R(c k ) GS j • g j , where T k = gj ∈R(c k ) GS j", "metadata": {"page": 5, "index_version": "2977684d0da4a8b6", "section_title": "Gaussian Attributes Vector Quantization", "file_name": "public-light.pdf", "chunk_index": 21, "title": "LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS", "id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "section_id": "section-7", "page_index": 4}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunkIndex": 21, "pageIndex": 4, "sectionId": "section-7", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "text": "Paper: LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS\n\nSection: Introduction\n\nContent:\nNovel view synthesis (NVS) aims to generate photo-realistic images of a 3D scene from unobserved viewpoints, given a set of calibrated multi-view images. This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360). Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes. Our Gaussian Pruning and Recovery method generalizes well, enhancing performance across different 3D Gaussian formats, such as Scaffold-GS.", "metadata": {"id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "page_index": 0, "title": "LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS", "section_title": "Introduction", "chunk_index": 0, "file_name": "public-light.pdf", "section_id": "section-1", "index_version": "2977684d0da4a8b6", "page": 1}, "similarity": null, "score": null, "pdfId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunkIndex": 0, "pageIndex": 0, "sectionId": "section-1", "sourceType": "current_paper"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "text": "Paper: LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS\n\nSection: More Experiment Results\n\nContent:\nof each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation. Overall comparisons with previous methods are listed in Table7, where we observe our LightGaussian markedly reduces the average storage size from 52.38MB to 7.89MB, while improving the FPS from 310 to 411 with only a slight rendering quality decrease.\nAdditional Qualitative Results on Mip-NeRF360. We provide extra visualizations for 3D-GS[16], LightGaussian (ours), and VQ-DVGO[49], accompanied by the corresponding residual maps from the We re-train 3D-GS, Compressed 3D-GS, Compact 3D-GS using their original code and 3D-GS configurations on our platform, to perform a fair comparison. We present the rendering results from 3D-GS[16], LightGaussian, and VQ-DVGO[49]. The residual maps highlight the differences between the rendered images and ground truth (GT) images.", "metadata": {"id": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "title": "LightGaussian: Unbounded 3D Gaussian Compression with 15x Reduction and 200+ FPS", "page": 16, "page_index": 15, "file_name": "public-light.pdf", "section_id": "section-16", "chunk_index": 35, "index_version": "2977684d0da4a8b6", "section_title": "More Experiment Results"}, "similarity": 0.860434889793396, "score": null, "pdfId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf", "chunkIndex": 35, "pageIndex": 15, "sectionId": "section-16", "sourceType": "current_paper"}], "groundedClaims": [{"summary": "在3DGS中，场景由一组3D高斯表示，每个高斯包含位置、透明度/不透明度参数α和协方差Σ。论文同时优化球谐系数来表示颜色c，以捕捉视角相关的外观。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-34", "quote": "In addition to positions 𝑝, 𝛼, and covariance Σ, we also optimize SH coefficients representing color 𝑐 of each Gaussian to correctly capture the view-dependent appearance of the scene."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "First, starting from sparse points produced during camera calibration, we represent the scene with 3D Gaussians that preserve desirable properties of continuous volumetric radiance fields for scene optimization while avoiding unnecessary computation in empty space;"}]}, {"summary": "原始3DGS通过密集各向异性高斯优化和快速光栅化追求高质量与实时渲染；LightGaussian则在3DGS基础上引入剪枝、低阶球谐蒸馏与矢量量化，以较小视觉质量代价换取更小的表示规模和更高FPS。", "kind": "inference", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "quote": "of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes."}]}, {"summary": "原始3DGS报告其各向异性高斯能够以较少参数建模复杂形状，但现有片段未给出与LightGaussian同条件的存储规模对比。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian作者报告大幅压缩（原文示例从782MB到45MB），并在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}, {"summary": "原始3DGS报告在1080p分辨率下实现实时新视角合成，给出作者主张的≥30 fps阈值。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian作者报告在复杂场景上渲染速度提升至超过200 FPS。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}, {"summary": "原始3DGS报告其辐射场质量与质量最佳的先前方法相当，并称在较长训练下达到最先进质量。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0", "quote": "Our method achieves real-time rendering of radiance fields with quality that equals the previous method with the best quality[Barron et al. 2022], while only requiring optimization times competitive with the fastest previous methods[Fridovich-Keil and Yu et al. 2022;Müller et al. 2022]."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0", "quote": "Note that for comparable training times to InstantNGP[Müller et al. 2022], we achieve similar quality to theirs; while this is the maximum quality they reach, by training for 51min we achieve state-of-the-art quality, even slightly better than Mip-NeRF360[Barron et al. 2022]."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "作者报告在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007，并称方法在FPS、模型大小与渲染质量之间取得最佳平衡。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}, {"summary": "原始3DGS通过各向异性协方差优化与密度控制构造精确场景，并开发可见性感知渲染以加速训练与支持实时渲染。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Third, we develop a fast visibility-aware rendering algorithm that supports anisotropic splatting and both accelerates training and allows realtime rendering."}], "paperId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf"}, {"summary": "LightGaussian通过全局显著性剪枝、从全阶球谐教师到低阶学生的蒸馏以及矢量量化来减少冗余，从而在规模、速度和质量之间取得平衡。", "kind": "reported", "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "quote": "of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation."}], "paperId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf"}], "sentenceSourceMap": [{"id": "grounded-1", "target": "message", "sentence": "在3DGS中，场景由一组3D高斯表示，每个高斯包含位置、透明度/不透明度参数α和协方差Σ。论文同时优化球谐系数来表示颜色c，以捕捉视角相关的外观。", "sourceIds": ["f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-34", "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2"], "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-34", "quote": "In addition to positions 𝑝, 𝛼, and covariance Σ, we also optimize SH coefficients representing color 𝑐 of each Gaussian to correctly capture the view-dependent appearance of the scene."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "First, starting from sparse points produced during camera calibration, we represent the scene with 3D Gaussians that preserve desirable properties of continuous volumetric radiance fields for scene optimization while avoiding unnecessary computation in empty space;"}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-2", "target": "message", "sentence": "原始3DGS通过密集各向异性高斯优化和快速光栅化追求高质量与实时渲染；LightGaussian则在3DGS基础上引入剪枝、低阶球谐蒸馏与矢量量化，以较小视觉质量代价换取更小的表示规模和更高FPS。", "sourceIds": ["f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0"], "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;"}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "quote": "of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "inference"}, {"id": "grounded-3", "target": "message", "sentence": "原始3DGS报告其各向异性高斯能够以较少参数建模复杂形状，但现有片段未给出与LightGaussian同条件的存储规模对比。", "sourceIds": ["f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64"], "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-64", "quote": "In comparison to previous explicit scene representations, the anisotropic Gaussians used in our optimization are capable of modelling complex shapes with a lower number of parameters."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-4", "target": "message", "sentence": "LightGaussian作者报告大幅压缩（原文示例从782MB到45MB），并在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "sourceIds": ["803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0"], "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-5", "target": "message", "sentence": "原始3DGS报告在1080p分辨率下实现实时新视角合成，给出作者主张的≥30 fps阈值。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "sourceIds": ["f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1"], "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-1", "quote": "We introduce three key elements that allow us to achieve state-of-the-art visual quality while maintaining competitive training times and importantly allow high-quality real-time (≥ 30 fps) novel-view synthesis at 1080p resolution."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-6", "target": "message", "sentence": "LightGaussian作者报告在复杂场景上渲染速度提升至超过200 FPS。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "sourceIds": ["803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0"], "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "Rendering speed also improves, reaching over 200 FPS on complex scenes."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-7", "target": "message", "sentence": "原始3DGS报告其辐射场质量与质量最佳的先前方法相当，并称在较长训练下达到最先进质量。", "sourceIds": ["f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0"], "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0", "quote": "Our method achieves real-time rendering of radiance fields with quality that equals the previous method with the best quality[Barron et al. 2022], while only requiring optimization times competitive with the fastest previous methods[Fridovich-Keil and Yu et al. 2022;Müller et al. 2022]."}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-0", "quote": "Note that for comparable training times to InstantNGP[Müller et al. 2022], we achieve similar quality to theirs; while this is the maximum quality they reach, by training for 51min we achieve state-of-the-art quality, even slightly better than Mip-NeRF360[Barron et al. 2022]."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-8", "target": "message", "sentence": "作者报告在Mip-NeRF 360上SSIM仅下降0.007，并称方法在FPS、模型大小与渲染质量之间取得最佳平衡。（作者报告，未作同条件比较）", "sourceIds": ["803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21"], "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-0", "quote": "This capability has widespread applications In summary, LightGaussian achieves substantial compression (e.g., from 782MB to 45MB) while maintaining visual fidelity (SSIM decrease of only 0.007 on Mip-NeRF 360)."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-21", "quote": "method strikes a balance among FPS, model size, and rendering quality, achieving the best balance among efficient representations."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-9", "target": "message", "sentence": "原始3DGS通过各向异性协方差优化与密度控制构造精确场景，并开发可见性感知渲染以加速训练与支持实时渲染。", "sourceIds": ["f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2"], "references": [{"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Second, we perform interleaved optimization/density control of the 3D Gaussians, notably optimizing anisotropic covariance to achieve an accurate representation of the scene;"}, {"sourceId": "f4c0c9f27e2d02b0265017f66049d471eb66cb50203bc918f51ba07d20cbbe11.pdf-chunk-2", "quote": "Third, we develop a fast visibility-aware rendering algorithm that supports anisotropic splatting and both accelerates training and allows realtime rendering."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}, {"id": "grounded-10", "target": "message", "sentence": "LightGaussian通过全局显著性剪枝、从全阶球谐教师到低阶学生的蒸馏以及矢量量化来减少冗余，从而在规模、速度和质量之间取得平衡。", "sourceIds": ["803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35"], "references": [{"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-13", "quote": "pruning strategy for 3D Gaussian Splatting to reduce over-parameterized points while maintaining accuracy."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-17", "quote": "Knowledge is distilled from a teacher model with full-degree SHs to a student model with truncated, lower-degree SHs."}, {"sourceId": "803219bf205d0142621b1ac5339f8d918d3f883f814559f6336b8bfdec5ca634.pdf-v2977684d0da4a8b6-chunk-35", "quote": "of each Gaussian, work to reduce the SH redundancy, and apply the Vector Quantization (codebook size set at 8192) to the learned representation."}], "method": "literal_quote", "kind": "reported"}]}}}
